# Tutorial-enabled Windows v0.2.1 release
Workstream-ID: lea-15
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/15
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed tutorial packaging, release publication and documentation scope
Status: DONE
Milestone: Deliver the guided tutorial in a verified downloadable Windows release
Dependencies: lea-12, lea-14

## Purpose
Publish the completed read-only desktop tutorial in a new Windows x64 release.
Keep source and packaged usage documentation aligned while preserving private
configuration and the immutable earlier release.

## Tasks
- [x] Review the existing tag-gated pipeline, public source and release authority.
- [x] Select an unused version and align package metadata, README and usage guides.
- [x] Include the guide and first-run instructions in the explicit public bundle.
- [x] Qualify release source and the actual frozen GUI/CLI offline.
- [x] Commit and push only reviewed public changes with repository-local attribution.
- [x] Publish the matching version tag through the existing qualified pipeline.
- [x] Verify the exact hosted run, downloaded integrity files and all bundled files.
- [x] Exercise downloaded normal GUI and standalone tutorial startup natively.
- [x] Reconcile issue, Project and persistent backlink, then deliver the release URL.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] The version tag, package version and downloaded manifest identify one exact source.
- [x] Both Windows entrypoints can open the bundled tutorial without private setup.
- [x] The normal desktop, contextual guide and sibling CLI work from the real asset.
- [x] Standalone tutorial navigation does not initialize configuration/history or start automation.
- [x] README screenshots and setup commands match this release's capabilities.
- [x] Private inputs, authentication, runtime history and unrelated dirty work remain unpublished.
- [x] Existing settings are preserved and the prior version's assets are not replaced.
- [x] Hosted publication and downloaded verification are distinguished from human/live qualification.
- [x] The completed workstream has one issue, one Done Project item and a durable backlink.

## Completion evidence
The initial release and tag inventory contained v0.2.0 only; selected patch
version 0.2.1 without overwriting the earlier release. Reviewed the trusted-ref
pipeline, job-scoped publication token and explicit public packaging resources.
Package versions, README captions, tutorial commands and bundled first-run
instructions are aligned. Existing setup remains outside the downloadable app;
no background tracking, new LinkedIn application or invitation is authorized.
The first fresh full source gate passed lint, format and typing, then failed
with a Windows access violation/native heap-corruption exit after test
assertions. The non-GUI selection exited normally; GUI lifetime isolation and
correction preceded source qualification and publication.
GUI diagnostics found retained closed windows. A focused shutdown regression
failed before the correction: the standalone tutorial was not destroyed when
its event loop returned. Desktop startup now explicitly delivers owned-window
deletion before application shutdown; Qt fixtures share one session application
and clean up native widgets. The corrected full local gates passed Ruff,
Black and product typing, then 698 tests with exit zero and no retained
top-level Qt widgets. The unrelated untracked plugin was excluded from local
lint and remains unpublished. The exact native heap-corruption stack is not
claimed diagnosed.

Reviewed source 0c8c502b33f0a871ab481ecc8d82ba04612547c4 is committed/pushed
with repository-local attribution and required trailers. Exact-source main
qualification 42469500764 and tag qualification/publication 42470184527 both
succeeded, including source gates, Windows packaging and frozen offline smoke.
The annotated v0.2.1 tag dereferences to that source; the stable hosted release is:
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/releases/tag/v0.2.1

Downloaded all three actual assets and verified hosted digests, SHA256SUMS,
manifest source/platform, archive inventory and every file before and after
non-overwriting versioned installation. ZIP: 114514070 bytes (109.2 MiB);
extracted: 267411166 bytes (255.0 MiB), 450 files. ZIP SHA256:
403c9c637edd6ba41dfb4872b1215c081d0089bbc3befece2f09f833eba54289.
The bundled UTF-8 guide matches the source text and contains 21 topics;
line-ending normalization applies only to that text comparison, not integrity hashes.

The installed asset passed offline version/help/init/statistics/test-form,
CSV/XLSX, existing-config preservation, GUI/contextual-guide rendering,
Playwright driver and real sibling CLI child checks. Separate native Windows
checks opened responsive standalone tutorials through both EXEs without
creating their absent workspace. The normal GUI's targeted F1 guide opened
and closed, its parent stayed responsive, and all native processes exited zero
with no unexpected or automation child. Read-only navigation is additionally
covered by source tests. Native checks preserved the captured post-error
preference and exact timestamp; the immediately pre-error preference remains
unknown. Earlier isolation failures are not erased.

The prior v0.2.0 tag, release identity and all asset identities/sizes/digests
remain unchanged. Private setup, authentication, runtime history and the
unrelated plugin remain excluded. These are unsigned portable binaries using
installed Edge/Chrome, not fresh-machine, live-site or human visual qualification.
Scoped closure and settled tracking receipts belong in the excluded index/ledger.

